      "writtenOn": "2018-01-19T01:18:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This read / mask / write is potentially a problem. HOOKS tasks will call bd9995x_select_input_port() which does RMW of the same register, it can be preempted by the charger task which calls this function. We can either add a mutex or check / clear this bit in bd9995x_select_input_port().\n\nI think clearing this bit in bd9995x_select_input_port() achieves the same function since VSYS_PRIORITY is only relevant when VSYSREG_SET \u003c\u003d VBAT, and we set VSYSREG to battery voltage_min in bd9995x_charger_enable(). So, if battery is super low when we start charging, we\u0027ll leave VSYSREG_SET on, but it will do nothing once battery voltage passes voltage_min. Then when we switch ports (eg. unplug) we\u0027ll clear VSYSREG_SET once and for all.\n\nWhat do you think?",
      "range": {
